{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cc714ea573ced272cbeb576a988e9871a9849c3b98bf7c627101d0958b54c72f","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot retrigger mechanism","key_entities":["retrigger.py","TRIGGER_TOKEN","_TOKEN_RE","_RETIRED_TOKEN_RE","recheck-review","rerun-llm-review","infra/gerrit/gerrit_to_platform.ini.template","_ACCEPTED_MESSAGE","_refusal_message","post_comment","src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py","tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger.py","app.py:176","reconcile.py:25"],"problem_keywords":["trigger collision","ci dispatch","gerrit chatops","comment matcher","substring matching","trigger word rename","bot reply injection"],"propositions":["The retired trigger word 'recheck-review' is a substring of the external CI ChatOps key 'recheck', causing substring-based matchers to collide and cancel in-flight CI runs.","The bot's own reply texts (_ACCEPTED_MESSAGE and _refusal_message) embedded the retired trigger word verbatim, re-dispatching the Verified workflow from bot-posted Gerrit comments.","A new trigger token 'rerun-llm-review' was chosen to share no substring in either direction with any [mapping \"comment-added\"] key in the ini template, enabling hard cutover without collision.","The retired word now queues no review, writes no label, and posts exactly one refusal reply placed after project guard and change re-anchoring, naming the new trigger word without spelling the old one."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787616888469396697,"uuid":"cccb03fc-ea7e-41b4-8a7b-08cc12efa89a"}